  "principle": "Territory is a canonical dimension independent from yearly documentary editions. Hubs exist for reader navigation, SEO and aggregation. Regions are agronomic documentary leaves: the smallest stable territories to which research coverage and documentary records are assigned. A hub may contain one or several leaves. A hub of several leaves may carry its own optional documentary layer (data/editions/<year>/hubs/<iso>/<hub>.json) for instruments shown to apply to every one of its leaves, which inherit it; a hub of one leaf is that leaf and never carries records of its own.",
